> > > > > > > > > >
> > > > > > > > > > More 'familiar' models like the M-model extension of the Leroux CAR give
> > > > > > > > > > indeed different results. The LCAR is closely based both in terms of
> > > > > > > > > > prior
> > > > > > > > > > choice and coding on the bigDM package, which implements some M-models
> > > > > > > > > > in
> > > > > > > > > > INLA and is documented in a paper by Vicente et al. (2023)
> > > > > > > > > >
> > > > > > > > > > In both cases (LCAR and BYM) I use a Uniform prior on the mixing
> > > > > > > > > > parameter
> > > > > > > > > > (precision mixing and variance mixing respectively) and  the Bartlett
> > > > > > > > > > decomposition on the covariance matrix, as outlined by Vicente et a.
> > > > > > > > > > (2023).
